1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,720
Hello friends, welcome to your channel HSC Study Guide.

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:12,640
In today's video, we will talk about how to get a safe working distance from the O-RAID electrical transmission line.

3
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,840
So let's start the video.

4
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:20,320
First of all, you should know what is the high voltage transmission line.

5
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:23,840
First of all, there are HV, i.e. High Voltage Lines.

6
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:31,680
So in this high voltage transmission line, the voltage level is up to 230 KV per 100 KV.

7
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:36,560
So this voltage comes under HV, i.e. comes under High Voltage.

8
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:40,400
Then there is EHV, i.e. Extra High Voltage Line.

9
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:46,480
So the voltage level in this is up to 230 KV per 1000 KV.

10
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:50,640
Third is UHV, i.e. Ultra High Voltage Line.

11
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:55,040
So the level of voltage in this is above 1000 KV.

12
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:59,280
So it is called UHV, i.e. Ultra High Voltage Line.

13
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:05,440
So in this way, there is a high voltage transmission line, which is quite important for you to know.

14
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:11,040
So let's know how safe working distance should be from the O-RAID power line.

15
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:18,560
So if the voltage is up to 11 KV, then we have to keep a safe working distance of 1.40 m.

16
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:28,400
Second is that if the voltage is up to 33 KV with 11 KV, then we have to keep a safe working distance of 3.60 m.

17
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:38,400
Third is that if the voltage is up to 132 KV with 33 KV, then we have to keep a safe working distance of 4.70 m.

18
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:50,000
After that, if the voltage is up to 232 KV with 233 KV, then we have to keep a safe working distance of 5.70 m.

19
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:01,280
And after that, if the voltage is up to 473 KV with 473 KV, then we have to maintain a safe working distance of 6.50 m.

20
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:07,600
So in this way, we have to maintain a safe working distance of O-RAID power line.

21
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:17,520
So friends, I hope that through this video, you got to know how safe working distance of O-RAID power line should be from the O-RAID power line.

22
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:22,560
So that's all for today, see you with another topic, till then take care, bye bye.
